%% Figure 4.8 - MQTT Asynchronous Publish/Subscribe Communication Flow
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ESP as ESP32-S3 Edge Node
    participant BRK as Mosquitto MQTT Broker (:1883)
    participant BACK as FastAPI Application Tier
    participant DB as SQLite & InfluxDB
    participant UI as React Presentation Tier

    Note over ESP,BRK: Network Initialization
    ESP->>BRK: Connect (ClientID: ESP32S3_MOTOR_NODE_01, KeepAlive: 60s)
    BRK-->>ESP: CONNACK (Connection Accepted)
    ESP->>BRK: Publish to [mems/motor001/status] (Online Heartbeat JSON)

    Note over BACK,BRK: Ingestion Pipeline Subscription
    BACK->>BRK: Connect & Subscribe to [mems/motor001/#]
    BRK-->>BACK: SUBACK (Granted QoS 0)

    Note over ESP,UI: 1Hz Periodic Telemetry Dispatch
    loop Every 1000 ms
        ESP->>BRK: Publish [mems/motor001/sensors] (Multi-Modal JSON)
        BRK->>BACK: Deliver [mems/motor001/sensors] (Async Thread Callback)
        BACK->>BACK: Validate Schema & Calculate Vector RMS & FFT
        BACK->>BACK: Check Thresholds & State Management
        par Dual Persistence
            BACK->>DB: Write to InfluxDB & SQLite
        and Real-Time Web Push
            BACK->>UI: Broadcast JSON via WebSocket (/ws/sensors)
        end
        UI->>UI: Update Live Charts, Gauges & Anomaly Alerts
    end

    opt Threshold Violation Detected
        BACK->>DB: Insert Active Alert Record
        BACK->>UI: Broadcast NEW_ALERT Event with Maintenance Action
        BACK->>BRK: Publish to [mems/motor001/alerts]
    end
